    "explanation": "To both parties — this is the decision on trip TRP-00204 (Jurong Point, 26 July 2026).\n\nNothing about the physical timeline is in dispute, and the platform's own records fix it. The driver accepted at 12:33:20, the trip record shows an 'arrived' event at 12:41:50, and the GPS trace places him inside the 120 m arrival radius for this LARGE_VENUE pickup at that moment (closest approach 94.94 m; 35 qualifying in-geofence fixes). He then held position for a continuous 340 seconds against a 300-second minimum and cancelled at 12:47:30 with reason code RIDER_UNREACHABLE. The arrival marker is not false: when he tapped he was inside the geofence and stationary, not more than 300 m away and not travelling at 15 km/h or more, so POL-NS-05 does not engage. On that footing the four limbs of POL-NS-01 are made out and the SGD 4.00 fee would stand, with SGD 3.20 to the driver under POL-NS-07.\n\nPOL-NS-01, however, charges the fee only where no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, and POL-NS-04 does. The rider was at the pin and actively trying to coordinate, and the driver did not answer her; the failed pickup is therefore a driver-side coordination failure, not a rider no-show. Each limb holds on the record: (a) her 12:44:40 message, 'boss? i still cannot see u leh', falls inside the 12:41:50–12:47:30 waiting window and is a statement that she could not see the vehicle, which POL-NS-04(a) names as locating content; (b) the chat log contains no driver message at all and trip_record.in_app_calls is empty — both of her messages were read (12:41:22 and 12:44:52) and neither drew a reply within 120 seconds, and no in-app call was placed before he terminated the trip; (c) her GPS track carries 105 qualifying fixes, every one within the 150 m LARGE_VENUE presence radius (maximum 39.93 m, mean 21.08 m). The driver's own submission accepts POL-NS-04 and confines the refund to the cancellation-fee line.\n\nMoney. The refund is SGD 4.00: the cancellation_fee line in fare_breakdown charged on 26 July 2026, which is also the greater of the SGD 4.00 LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee and the SGD 4.00 RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee, and is the whole of the amount contested. The SGD 0.50 platform fee is a separate ledger line and is not part of the contested amount, so it is not refunded. No driver compensation is payable, because POL-NS-04 displaces the POL-NS-01/POL-NS-07 entitlement.\n\nIntegrity and escalation. No POL-NS-08 defect fires: the arrival event and the first in-geofence fix share the same timestamp 12:41:50 (no clock skew), the trace has 87 fixes with no gap at all (max_gap_sec 0.0), the chat log's 3 messages match trip_record.chat_message_count of 3 with an unbroken message sequence, and the SGD 4.00 fee line reconciles with the fee schedule. No POL-NS-09 trigger fires: confidence is above the 0.70 floor, no admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence (the driver's RIDER_UNREACHABLE status is answered by POL-NS-04, which reads the chat log as its own test), the two profiles show no repeat disputes between these parties (0 and 0), and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip — 3 no-show terminations in 30 days is below the absolute count of 4, and 3/142 = 0.021 is below the 0.08 rate. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00204-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0) and is not relied on; POL-NS-06 is not engaged because the dwell was 340 seconds, 40 seconds over the minimum.\n\nOne detail noted but immaterial: the filed narrative says 'Entrance 1', while the message on file says Entrance 3, matching the registered pickup point 'Jurong Point, PHV Pickup Point, Entrance 3'. No limb turns on it."
