    "explanation": "To both parties: the record is consistent and this case can be decided now.\n\nFor the driver: on the platform's own telemetry the baseline conditions of POL-NS-01 were met. You reached the pickup geofence at 12:41:50 (closest approach 94.94 m, inside the 120 m arrival radius fixed for this LARGE_VENUE pin), held position for a continuous 340 seconds against the 300-second minimum, and terminated the trip at 12:47:30 with no boarding and the reason code RIDER_UNREACHABLE. On that baseline the SGD 4.00 charge would stand and you would be owed SGD 3.20 (80 percent of SGD 4.00).\n\nBut POL-NS-04 displaces that baseline, and it is made out on the chat log and the rider's track, which you do not contest. The rider sent two locating messages inside the attempt — 'hi im at the entrance 3 phv pickup point, which car ah?' at 12:41:05 and 'boss? i still cannot see u leh' at 12:44:40 — and both were delivered and read (read receipts 12:41:22 and 12:44:52). You posted no reply within 120 seconds of either message and placed no in-app call (trip_record.in_app_calls is empty). The rider's device stayed within 39.93 m of the pin at its furthest (mean 21.08 m) across all 105 qualifying fixes, inside the 150 m presence radius for this zone class. All three limbs of POL-NS-04 hold: the rider is exonerated, the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee is refunded in full, and no driver compensation is payable. POL-NS-04 provides no compensation, and by displacing POL-NS-01 it removes the basis for the SGD 3.20 claimed under POL-NS-07.\n\nFor the rider: you are refunded the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee charged at 12:47:48 on 2026-07-26. That figure is the greater of the SGD 4.00 LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee and the SGD 4.00 RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee, and it is the whole of the amount you contested. The SGD 0.50 platform fee in the same ledger is not part of the contested amount and is not refunded — the total charged was SGD 4.50, and the refund returns the cancellation-fee line only.\n\nNo POL-NS-05 false-arrival finding arises: your in-geofence stationary run begins exactly at the 12:41:50 arrival timestamp, inside the radius and at zero speed, and your claim to the contrary is rejected. Your written narrative refers to 'Entrance 1' while the message on file and the trip record both say 'Entrance 3'; the message governs and nothing turns on the discrepancy.\n\nNo escalation: no POL-NS-09 trigger is engaged — both parties show 0 counterparty disputes in 90 days, the rider has 0 no-show disputes in 30 days, and the driver's anti-farming figures (3 terminations against 142 completed trips in 30 days, a rate of 0.021) sit below both the absolute count of 4 and the 0.08 rate. No artifact carrying a deciding fact is impaired under POL-NS-08: arrival skew is 0 seconds against a 90-second tolerance, the trace has 87 fixes with an empty gaps array, the chat's 3 messages match the recorded chat_message_count with an unbroken sequence, and the SGD 4.00 fee line reconciles with the fee schedule. The only impaired artifact is EV-ADVIS-00204-01, the traffic advisory, at weight 0.0 because it is MISSING; it carries nothing this ruling rests on and bears only on POL-NS-06(i), which is unavailable on a missing advisory. No clause produces a referral, so none is listed."
